👑🧠 Birbal and the Two Merchants (Raw Story)

One day, two merchants came to Emperor Akbar.

They were arguing over a bag of gold coins.

The first merchant said, “This bag is mine. I earned it.”

The second said, “No, it belongs to me!”

Akbar asked Birbal to solve the problem.

Birbal took the bag and said, “I will find the truth.”

He secretly checked the bag and noticed it smelled of spices.

The next day, he called both merchants.

He asked the first merchant, “What do you do?”

“I am a spice seller,” he said.

Then he asked the second merchant, who said, “I sell clothes.”

Birbal smiled and said, “The bag belongs to the spice seller.”

Akbar agreed and gave the bag to the first merchant.

💖 Moral:

Truth can be found with careful observation.
